WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.808 --> 00:00:07.837
Aisha Coleman: Morning, Linda. How's your week going?

2
00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:15.960
Linda Sorensen: Morning, Aisha. Busy. Open enrollment stuff, plus we're short two people on the member care team, so I'm bouncing between floors.

3
00:00:16.623 --> 00:00:21.718
Aisha Coleman: Oh, that's a lot. Is that the Tacoma center or the Spokane one?

4
00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:28.845
Linda Sorensen: Tacoma. Spokane is fine. We had a couple of retirements, and hiring in financial services is slow right now.

5
00:00:29.716 --> 00:00:37.690
Aisha Coleman: Got it. Well, before we get into the QM stuff, I wanted to check on call volumes. How's October looking?

6
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:48.061
Linda Sorensen: We're at about 38,000 calls month to date, which is up maybe six percent from September. The Google Ads piece is doing its job, though I can't tell you why.

7
00:00:48.496 --> 00:00:54.838
Aisha Coleman: That's good to hear. And the Salesforce sync is still writing call records correctly? No missing outcomes?

8
00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:02.253
Linda Sorensen: As far as I know. Our Salesforce admin, Theresa, hasn't flagged anything. She would, loudly.

9
00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:10.392
Aisha Coleman: Ha. Okay. So what's on your mind for today? I know you wanted to talk about the renewal planning.

10
00:01:11.232 --> 00:01:33.305
Linda Sorensen: Yeah. Here's the thing. We're looking at a budget freeze for next fiscal year. Flat spend at best. And finance and procurement are pushing back hard on the way the add-ons are priced separately. PreSense, the QM seats, any AI Voice Agent minutes. They see three line items and they want one number.

11
00:01:34.016 --> 00:01:38.407
Aisha Coleman: That's fair. Can I ask what they're comparing it to?

12
00:01:39.257 --> 00:01:50.600
Linda Sorensen: Honestly, they're comparing it to what we already pay. They don't care that the add-ons are different products. They see a platform fee and then a bunch of extra charges.

13
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.759
Linda Sorensen: It makes the renewal conversation harder than it needs to be.

14
00:01:55.757 --> 00:02:07.037
Aisha Coleman: Okay. I can't promise anything on packaging, but I can bring that to our finance team and see what options exist for a single line item.

15
00:02:07.037 --> 00:02:08.339
Aisha Coleman: Would that help?

16
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:19.921
Linda Sorensen: It would. I'm not asking for a discount. I'm asking for fewer moving parts. If we can show procurement one number, we can probably get it through.

17
00:02:21.398 --> 00:02:33.927
Aisha Coleman: Understood. Let me take that back and see what's possible. No promises, but I'll get you an answer before your budget submission date, which I think is mid November?

18
00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.828
Linda Sorensen: November 14th. That's the hard deadline.

19
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:46.660
Aisha Coleman: Okay. I'll put a pin in that. Now, the other thing you mentioned in your email was the QM scorecard change process.

20
00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.365
Aisha Coleman: Can you tell me what's happening there?

21
00:02:49.958 --> 00:03:03.385
Linda Sorensen: It's not a problem with the tool. It's our compliance team. Every time we adjust a scorecard, they want to review it, and they want a record of who changed what and when.

22
00:03:03.385 --> 00:03:07.046
Linda Sorensen: Right now that's a manual screenshot process. It's slow.

23
00:03:08.463 --> 00:03:13.923
Aisha Coleman: Got it. So it's more of a workflow and audit trail thing on your side.

24
00:03:14.989 --> 00:03:25.856
Linda Sorensen: Yes. I don't need you to solve it today. I just wanted you to know why QM changes take us three weeks instead of three days.

25
00:03:27.052 --> 00:03:32.992
Aisha Coleman: That's helpful context. I'll note it. And how's the quality score trending? Are the scores themselves looking okay?

26
00:03:34.358 --> 00:03:38.727
Linda Sorensen: They're fine. The coaching conversations have been good. No complaints there.

27
00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:47.435
Aisha Coleman: Great. Anything else on the account side? I know you had a new member experience analyst start a few weeks ago.

28
00:03:47.928 --> 00:03:57.950
Linda Sorensen: Yes, Daniel. He's ramping on the Invoca reporting. He'll probably need a training session on the Signal AI Studio at some point, but not urgent.

29
00:03:58.293 --> 00:04:03.661
Aisha Coleman: I can do a session in November. I'll send a couple of dates.

30
00:04:04.255 --> 00:04:05.388
Linda Sorensen: That works. Thanks.

31
00:04:05.936 --> 00:04:15.679
Aisha Coleman: Okay. So to recap, I'm taking the billing structure question to our finance team and will get back to you before November 14th.

32
00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:20.762
Aisha Coleman: And I'll send training dates for Daniel. Anything else before we wrap?

33
00:04:21.774 --> 00:04:28.327
Linda Sorensen: No, that's it. Appreciate you listening on the pricing thing. I know it's not your call.

34
00:04:29.526 --> 00:04:32.294
Aisha Coleman: I'll do what I can. Talk soon, Linda.

35
00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.685
Linda Sorensen: Thanks, Aisha. Bye.
